Patch to the native two-pass solver of QuipNetwork/quip-solver-cuda PR #5 (contrib/native-two-pass, commit 97faa92).
The patched file is a derivative of that crate and is licensed, like it, under AGPL-3.0-or-later; the SPDX header of
solver.rs is unchanged. Adds two opt-in features to solver.rs only (no new dependencies; kernel.cu, Cargo.toml and
Cargo.lock untouched):
  - search-config keys struct_cutoff / struct_streams: a CPU structural prefilter in the native miner (E83);
  - a --serve mode: a persistent helper that answers solve requests on stdin/stdout (PROTOCOL.md, E84).
Without --serve and without struct_cutoff the solver behaves as PR #5 at 97faa92.
Apply from the root of a PR #5 checkout:  patch -p1 < pr5-serve.patch

